1. DEFINITIONS

1.1 "Software" means the thunderstrike client libraries published by the
    Licensor in any form, including the compiled native libraries, the
    language adapters and packages that accompany them (for Go, Rust,
    Python, Node.js, .NET, Java, PHP, C and C++), their header files, the
    documentation, and any update, upgrade or new version of any of them
    that the Licensor makes available.

1.2 "Compiled Libraries" means the parts of the Software distributed only
    in object-code form, such as static and shared libraries and native
    addons.

1.3 "Adapters" means the parts of the Software distributed in source form
    in a programming language other than that of the Compiled Libraries,
    which call the Compiled Libraries.

1.4 "Your Application" means a software application or service that you
    develop, which uses the Software to communicate with a thunderstrike
    server, and which adds substantial functionality of its own beyond the
    Software.

1.5 "Third-Party Components" means software owned by third parties that is
    included in the Software and licensed under its own terms, as listed in
    the notices described in Section 7.

